<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 5.69 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 5.69 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.5550 to the dollar, down from 3.3830 on Monday and at 1.9780 to the mark, down from 1.8885, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 5.69 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, nearly five-percent weaker than Monday's fix at -0.77 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
